  "notes": "Single-page-group invoice on two pages; the line-item table (full grid) continues on page 2 and its header row is repeated there by the author, listed once. The small line \"Invoice INV-2026-04418, continued\" at the top of page 2 is a continuation note, neither body nor furniture in expected; a scorer should ignore it. Section rows (\"Section A — Glassware\" etc.) span all six columns and totals labels span five; their text is repeated in every covered cell. Description cells hold two lines joined with one space. The BILL TO and SHIP TO boxes stand side by side; reading order is box by box (left box entirely, then right box). Their address lines are not key sentences; the italic sentence closing each box is. The boxed key/value panel (invoice number, dates) and the remittance key/value table have no header row. List markers in \"Payment terms\" are drawn by CSS (disc, nested circle). Letterhead lines repeat on both pages and are listed once."
